Liquid Personnel is recruiting Social Worker for its client's Learning Disabilities Review Project Team at Cambridgeshire.

This is an excellent opportunity for a skilled practitioner to work within a county-wide specialist team supporting adults with Learning Disabilities and Autism (LD&amp;A). The role focuses on reviewing complex and high-cost care packages to ensure they continue to meet individual needs, deliver positive outcomes, promote independence, and provide value for public resources.&nbsp;

Working closely with Senior Social Workers, Contracts Teams, Brokerage Services, individuals, families, carers, and advocacy services, you will undertake comprehensive reviews and assessments of existing support arrangements. The successful candidate will be experienced in strengths-based and person-centred practice, with the ability to analyse complex situations and make evidence-based recommendations that improve outcomes and maximise wellbeing.&nbsp;

What will your responsibilities be?

• Completing Care Act 2014 assessments for adults with Learning Disabilities and Autism, including cases involving complex and high-cost care packages.&nbsp;

• Undertaking timely reviews following changes in an individual's needs, circumstances, or support arrangements.&nbsp;

• Reviewing care and support packages to ensure they remain proportionate, effective, outcome-focused, and represent value for money.

• Delivering a minimum of two completed and recorded assessments per week.&nbsp;

• Conducting face-to-face assessments and reviews with individuals and their support networks.&nbsp;

• Working closely with advocates, carers, families, providers, and partner agencies to ensure a person-centred approach to assessment and care planning.

• Analysing and evaluating care and support arrangements to identify strengths, risks, gaps, and opportunities for improved outcomes.&nbsp;

• Collaborating with Contracts and Brokerage Teams to develop cost-effective and appropriate support solutions.

• Promoting independence, wellbeing, choice, and control through strengths-based interventions and support planning.

• Undertaking Mental Capacity Assessments and contributing to Best Interest decision-making where required.

• Maintaining accurate, defensible, and timely records, assessments, reviews, and professional reports.&nbsp;

Qualifications &amp; Experience:

To be successful in this role you must have,&nbsp;

• Professional Qualification:&nbsp;MA, BA, BSc in Social Work, Diploma in Social Work, CQSW, or equivalent recognised Social Work qualification.

• Registration:&nbsp;Must be registered with Social Work England.&nbsp;

• Experience:&nbsp;Significant post-qualified experience within Adult Social Care.

• Learning Disabilities &amp; Autism Experience:&nbsp;Proven experience working with adults with Learning Disabilities and Autism.&nbsp;

• Legislation Knowledge:&nbsp;Strong understanding of the Care Act 2014 and Mental Capacity Act 2005.

• Assessment Skills:&nbsp;Experience undertaking complex assessments, reviews, and evaluations of care and support arrangements.&nbsp;

• Care Package Reviews:&nbsp;Experience reviewing complex and high-cost care packages and making evidence-based recommendations.&nbsp;

• Multi-Agency Working:&nbsp;Strong experience working collaboratively with brokerage teams, contracts teams, providers, carers, advocates, and partner agencies.&nbsp;

• Communication Skills:&nbsp;Excellent assessment, analytical, report-writing, and professional communication skills.

• Driving Licence:&nbsp;Access to your own vehicle is essential.

